# Accessibility & WCAG AA Compliance Rule

When generating or modifying frontend UI components, you **MUST** encode accessibility directly into the markup:

## 1. Color Contrast & Readability in Dark Mode
- All body text in obsidian dark mode (`#030712`) must maintain at least **4.5:1** contrast ratio (`#f9fafb` for headings, `#94a3b8` for descriptions).
- Avoid dark grey text on dark backgrounds (`#334155` text on `#0b0f19` background is strictly forbidden).

## 2. Interactive Focus Rings
- All interactive controls (buttons, links, inputs, tabs) must have visible focus rings for keyboard navigation:
  - `focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-gold-500/50 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-slate-950`

## 3. ARIA Semantics
- Custom interactive cards, tabs, and modals must include appropriate ARIA attributes (`aria-label`, `role="tab"`, `aria-selected="true"`).
